{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/fire_stand","webpackCompilationHash":"8cc9788010e3663b7336","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>The fire stand is designed as a display stand for my beaded bottles - blucka bluck, cna yoohoo, etc. The idea was to make a display that made it appear that the bottle was lit by campfire. A platform holding the bottle rotates, showing the bottle from all sides and also moving powered contacts around under a circle of LEDs which flicker with many colors. </p>\n<p><a href=\"/bottom-388b2e198d7383ef29400ae241c196a7.jpg\"><img src=\"/bottom-388b2e198d7383ef29400ae241c196a7.jpg\" title=\"bottom\"></a> </p>\n<p><a href=\"/side-d40c9afc82bda0e214f54a7ad6bf8524.jpg\"><img src=\"/side-d40c9afc82bda0e214f54a7ad6bf8524.jpg\" title=\"side\"></a> </p>\n<p><a href=\"/firestand-c9a9f54ae89e6d4dccacc01ad90fb55d.jpg\"><img src=\"/firestand-c9a9f54ae89e6d4dccacc01ad90fb55d.jpg\" title=\"firestand\"></a> </p>","frontmatter":{"path":"/fire_stand","title":"Fire Stand","date":"2003-11-28","tags":["artwork","beadwork","cna","electronics"]}}},"pageContext":{"isCreatedByStatefulCreatePages":false,"prev":{"html":"<p>This loom design is a stylized version of the drawings from <a href=\"http://www.zombie-and-mummy.org\">http://www.zombie-and-mummy.org</a> </p>\n<p>pattern:</p>\n<img src=\"/mummy-57a221120c2ceb455bc393b2b72bac11.gif\" width=\"300\"/> \n<p>off the loom: </p>\n<p><a href=\"/boom_boom_mummy_mummy_sm1-388c28be94e07e37c9d370b55968006e.jpg\"><img src=\"/boom_boom_mummy_mummy_sm1-388c28be94e07e37c9d370b55968006e.jpg\" title=\"boom_boom_mummy_mummy_sm1\"></a> </p>\n<p>framed: </p>\n<p><a href=\"/boom_boom_mummy_mummy_frame-e988594619f02dd560f1821d9c8cf73c.jpg\"><img src=\"/boom_boom_mummy_mummy_frame-e988594619f02dd560f1821d9c8cf73c.jpg\" title=\"boom_boom_mummy_mummy_frame\"></a>          </p>","id":"e37be2ca-c3a1-594f-b2ac-2384de659dcf","frontmatter":{"path":"/boom_boom_mummy_mummy","title":"Boom Boom Mummy Mummy","date":"2003-11-28","tags":["beadwork"],"hexagonImages":["boom_boom_mummy_mummy_sm1.jpg_hexagon.jpeg","boom_boom_mummy_mummy_frame.jpg_hexagon.jpeg"]}},"next":{"html":"<p>A series of square-stitch bracelets based on the audience graphics from the Commodore64 game Hardball the game: </p>\n<p><a href=\"/screenshot-2b59dce976ed6ca95b001f537b19d380.gif\"><img src=\"/screenshot-2b59dce976ed6ca95b001f537b19d380.gif\" title=\"screenshot\"></a> </p>\n<p>finished things: <a href=\"/hardball_bracelet-776ec4c9f9d5ce683e2b80d8caba158c.jpg\"><img src=\"/hardball_bracelet-776ec4c9f9d5ce683e2b80d8caba158c.jpg\" title=\"hardball_bracelet\"></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"/hardball2-b6d24236c771709eba487436948a0a3c.jpg\"><img src=\"/hardball2-b6d24236c771709eba487436948a0a3c.jpg\" title=\"hardball2\"></a><br>\n</p>","id":"65dcfe9d-0c09-5460-a832-d301b039a75a","frontmatter":{"path":"/hardball_bracelets","title":"Hardball Bracelets","date":"2003-11-28","tags":["beadwork","c64","cna"],"hexagonImages":["screenshot.gif_hexagon.png","hardball_bracelet.jpg_hexagon.jpeg","hardball2.jpg_hexagon.jpeg"]}}}}}